## Mail relay

All alert and cron email leaves through the single relay at `{{ smtp_host }}`.
An alert on it is usually the smarthost credential or the smarthost's own TLS
verification, not the local Postfix.

```bash
ssh {{ admin_user }}@{{ smtp_host }}
sudo systemctl status postfix
mailq                        # or: sudo postqueue -p
sudo tail -50 /var/log/mail.log
```

Three states matter:

| State | Reading | First move |
|---|---|---|
| Queue growing | mail is accepted and not delivered | the upstream hop, not Postfix |
| Deferred climbing | repeated delivery failures | `mail.log` for the SASL or TLS error |
| Relay unreachable | senders cannot hand mail over | the service, then the firewall between sender and relay |

After fixing the upstream, flush the queue rather than waiting out the retry
timer:

```bash
sudo postfix flush           # or: sudo postqueue -f
```

While the relay is down the email leg of every alert is blind. Any
non-email receiver is the only delivery path until it recovers.

