## kube-system fencing

`kube-system` is fenced like every other namespace: an ingress default-deny from
the `netpol-baseline` component plus a complete allow set, all of it in
`kubernetes/infrastructure/configs/kube-system-policies/`.

The deny is only safe while the allow set is complete, so the two must land in
the same reconcile and be reviewed together. kured is reconciled by the
controllers stage and CoreDNS and metrics-server by k3s itself; splitting the
policies to sit beside each workload would let the deny land while an allow's
stage is still pending. The `resources:` list is ordered allows-first because
kustomize emits in list order and the component appends the deny last.

**CoreDNS is the one allow that can break the cluster if it is narrowed.** A
query reaches those pods three ways, which is why one rule carries three peer
shapes:

- every namespace, the path almost all traffic takes;
- the pod CIDR, because a query aimed at the kube-dns ClusterIP from outside the
  pod network is DNAT'd and masqueraded by kube-proxy and can arrive as the
  sending node's flannel gateway address;
- the LAN, as defence in depth for host-netns clients.

The last two widen nothing: neither pod IPs nor the ClusterIP are LAN-routable,
and the pod CIDR is a subset of what the namespace selector already admits.
Confirm no host-side unit queries the cluster DNS ClusterIP before narrowing the
LAN peer.

metrics-server's allow is label-scoped to `k8s-app: metrics-server`, the k3s
AddOn's label. Replacing the AddOn with the upstream chart needs a second policy
selecting `app.kubernetes.io/name: metrics-server`; NetworkPolicies are
additive, so two objects cover both label sets.

Current residents and their ingress: CoreDNS `53/udp`+`53/tcp` from everything
and `9153` from observability; metrics-server `10250` from the aggregation
layer; kured `8080` from observability; kube-vip is hostNetwork, which
NetworkPolicy never gates. `local-storage` sits in `k3s_disable`, so there is no
local-path-provisioner and no default StorageClass: a PVC that omits
`storageClassName` stays Pending. Adding a workload here means adding its allow
in the same commit.

